{"step_index":193,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T19:08:36Z","thinking":"**Considering Security Options**\n\nI'm currently weighing security implementation choices. It's a question of utilizing the `itsdangerous` library, which is already integrated within the Pallets ecosystem, or developing a custom HMAC-SHA256 session token serializer. I'm leaning toward the standard library approach. I'm focusing on `hmac`, `hashlib`, `base64`, `json`, and `time`.\n\n\n**Analyzing Security Design**\n\nI've determined that `base64` is preferable due to its lack of dependencies and compatibility with Vercel serverless functions. I've formulated a simple session token structure: base64-encoded JSON payload concatenated with a base64-encoded HMAC-SHA256 signature. Verification involves decoding, recomputing the HMAC, and checking expiration via `hmac.compare_digest`. I'm setting an `httponly`, `samesite`, and `secure` cookie.\n\n\n**Implementing Access Control**\n\nI'm now implementing the access control logic, constructing a `verify_paid_session` FastAPI dependency. This dependency checks for the presence and validity of the `streamwave_session` cookie, decoding it and verifying its integrity. I'm raising HTTP exceptions for missing or invalid sessions, and using the dependency to protect the media endpoints: `/api/media`, `/api/media/{media_id}`, and `/api/play-events`. Unprotected endpoints include `/api/health`, `/api/session`, `/api/demo-payment`, `/api/logout`, and `/api/reset-demo`, along with documentation and static HTML routes.\n\n\n**Designing Checkout Functionality**\n\nI'm now designing the checkout process and payment simulation. My focus is on creating a user-friendly experience that mirrors a real transaction without processing any actual payments. I'm prioritizing clarity, ensuring that all demonstration elements are clearly marked as such to avoid any confusion for the user. I'm focusing on the `/checkout` page, specifically how the EcoCash and Visa/Mastercard options are presented.\n\nI'm making sure that the page automatically populates with the user's email, and uses simulation payment flows that are smooth for the user.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":true,\"Summary\":\"Implementation Plan for StreamWave Landing Page, EcoCash/Visa/MasterCard Academic Payment Simulation, and Cookie-Based Paid Member Access Control.\",\"UserFacing\":true}","CodeContent":"\"# Implementation Plan - StreamWave Landing Page, Simulated Checkout & Paid Member Access Control\\n\\nExtend the existing **StreamWave Entertainment** FastAPI serverless application on Vercel by adding an original public landing page, simulated subscription-payment checkout (EcoCash, Visa, MasterCard), signed cookie session management, and protected member access control for `/library`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## User Review Required\\n\\n> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> **Academic Simulation Safety**: This is a non-commercial academic demonstration. No real money will be transferred and no actual financial information (card numbers, CVVs, PINs, mobile payment PINs) will be collected, transmitted, or logged.\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Access Control Model**: Catalogue browsing (`/api/media`), detail lookups (`/api/media/{id}`), and playback event logging (`/api/play-events`) will be protected by FastAPI signed session cookies. The `/api/health` and `/docs` endpoints remain publicly accessible for automated assessment checks.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Proposed Changes\\n\\n### Configuration & Central Subscription Settings\\n\\n#### [MODIFY] [`app.py`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/app.py)\\n- Define a single subscription configuration source of truth:\\n  ```python\\n  SUBSCRIPTION_PLAN = {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"streamwave-monthly\\\",\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"StreamWave Monthly\\\",\\n      \\\"price\\\": \\\"US$2.99\\\",\\n      \\\"price_amount\\\": 2.99,\\n      \\\"currency\\\": \\\"USD\\\",\\n      \\\"interval\\\": \\\"month\\\"\\n  }\\n  ```\\n- Implement secure session cookie signature logic using `DEMO_SESSION_SECRET` env var with a fallback.\\n- Implement FastAPI reusable dependency `verify_paid_session` to protect `/api/media`, `/api/media/{media_id}`, and `/api/play-events`.\\n- Add new endpoints:\\n  - `GET /api/session`: Checks active session cookie status.\\n  - `POST /api/demo-payment`: Validates email, plan, and payment method (`ecocash`, `visa`, `mastercard`), generates reference `SW-DEMO-XXXXX`, logs structured JSON event, and sets `streamwave_session` \n<truncated 4793 bytes>","Description":"\"Create implementation plan for landing page, checkout simulation, and session access control\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\dell\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457\\\\implementation_plan.md\"","toolAction":"\"Creating implementation plan\"","toolSummary":"\"Creating implementation plan\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
